ostrya (0.10.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * remote gpg-import reads each -k file as a binary or an ASCII-armored
    keyring by itself. A mix of binary and armored files imports.
  * remote gpg-import and remote add --gpg-import refuse key input over
    4 MiB before they read all of it.
  * remote gpg-import and remote add --gpg-import read the repository
    keyring through a symlink, and take a symlink to no file as no
    keyring. They refuse a repository keyring over 4 MiB before they read
    it.
  * The collection-id of a repository is its local namespace. refs -c
    --create and pull --collection write refs/heads/REF for that id.
  * refs -c, summary -u, and the ref listing of serve ignore
    refs/mirrors/ID/ of the own collection id. fsck prints a line for
    each ref there, and prune keeps its commit.
  * push to a bucket and remote summary -u skip the keys of
    refs/mirrors/ID/ of the collection id of the bucket. remote fsck
    gives each such key a note, and remote prune keeps its commit.
  * A revision takes @ID:NAME, the ref NAME of the collection ID. An
    error names a collection ref as @ID:NAME.
  * commit -b and --tag take @ID:NAME. The refs of one commit are in one
    namespace, and ostree.collection-binding holds its id. --tag refuses
    a remote ref.
  * refs --create and refs --delete take @ID:NAME without -c. A PREFIX
    @ID: matches each ref of the collection ID, and a listing prints
    @ID:NAME. -A refuses a collection ref of another id.
  * prune --only-branch and --retain-branch-depth take @ID:NAME.
  * pull-local takes @ID:REF operands of more than one collection.
  * A client group holds the items of each namespace: allow takes
    [MODES:]@ID:PATTERN, and deny takes @ID:PATTERN. The config refuses
    the key collection, and one item in two groups. With no client
    group, the one implicit group is anonymous.
  * A claim is ostrya:ref:[MODES:]@ID:PATTERN or ostrya:ref:!@ID:PATTERN
    for the collection ID. serve refuses a certificate with an
    ostrya:collection: URI with 403.

 -- Alexey Naidyonov <alexey.naidyonov@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 15:15:21 +0100

ostrya (0.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * pull --collection reads a file:// candidate as a local repository.
    It hashes each object it imports from such a candidate when the keys
    of the candidate check the signatures of the commits or the summary.
  * pull --collection skips a listed ref whose name fails the ref-name
    rule, with a warning.
  * pull --collection prints the pull-local statistics line for the
    objects it imports from local candidates.
  * pull --collection under the own collection id writes
    refs/mirrors/ID/REF when that file holds a ref, and refs/heads/REF
    otherwise.
  * refs -c --delete checks each ref before it deletes a ref, and
    refuses a local name with ':'.

 -- Alexey Naidyonov <alexey.naidyonov@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 14:46:14 +0100

ostrya (0.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * commit --tree=tar gives the uid, gid, and xattr records of a pax
    global header to the members that follow it.
  * commit --tree=tar refuses a symlink member whose size is not 0.
  * commit --tree=tar reports a header field that is not valid UTF-8 as
    an i/o error.

